# Cursor Rules for Laravel Backend Project

## Role

Act as a senior backend developer specialized in PHP 8.2+ and Laravel 12.
Focus on clean, maintainable and pragmatic solutions. Avoid overengineering.

## General Principles

* Always follow clean code principles (SOLID)
* Never put business logic inside controllers
* Prefer service classes for core logic
* Keep controllers thin

## Architecture

* Use Laravel MVC structure
* Business logic goes in app/Services
* Validation goes in Form Requests
* Use Eloquent relationships properly
* Keep architecture simple and practical

## Coding Standards

* Use `declare(strict_types=1);` in all PHP files
* All methods must have explicit parameter and return types
* Follow PSR-12 coding style
* Use clear and descriptive naming

## Naming Convention

* Class, method and variable names must ALWAYS be in English
* Use domain-driven names (e.g. `DamageCalculator`, `BattleService`)
* Comments and explanations can be written in Spanish

## API Design

* Follow RESTful conventions
* Return JSON responses
* Use proper HTTP status codes

## Database

* Use migrations for schema
* Use seeders for test data
* Prefer relationships over manual queries

## Testing

* Write unit tests for services when possible
* Focus on testing business logic

## Project-Specific Rules

* Pokemon battle logic must be isolated in a service
* Damage calculation must be reusable and testable
* Avoid hardcoding values
* Keep battle state consistent and predictable

## AI Interaction

* Do not generate large files without explanation
* Prefer step-by-step generation
* Ask for clarification if context is missing
* Prefer simple and clean solutions over complex architectures
